  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to freeze, to cower, to be paralyzed with fear",
      "explanation": "To become unable to move or act due to fear, shock, or nervousness. The body stiffens and one cannot take action."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10356_sukumu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{恐怖|きょうふ}で{足|あし}がすくんだ。",
      "english": "My legs froze with fear.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10356_sukumu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{大|おお}きな{犬|いぬ}に{吠|ほ}えられて{体|からだ}がすくんだ。",
      "english": "A big dog barked at me and I froze up.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10356_sukumu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{高|たか}いところから{下|した}を{見|み}たら、{足|あし}がすくんで{一歩|いっぽ}も{動|うご}けなくなった。",
      "english": "When I looked down from the high place, my legs froze and I couldn't move a single step.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {足|あし}がすくむ: one's legs freeze/give way (most common)\n- {体|からだ}がすくむ: one's body freezes\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}ですくむ: to freeze with fear\n\nPAIR: すくむ（{自動詞|じどうし}）↔ すくめる（{他動詞|たどうし}）= to shrug, to hunch (as in {肩|かた}をすくめる)\n\nUSAGE: Most commonly used in the pattern {足|あし}がすくむ to describe being unable to move due to fear, especially of heights.",
